<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex details Q1 income, sales.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex details Q1 income, sales.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) reported its first quarter consolidated income statement. Figures in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>    Item				  Q1 1996		Q1 1997</p>
<p>  Total Sales			    6,306		  7,876</p>
<p>  Domestic Sales			 3,862		  4,967</p>
<p>  Export Sales			   2,444		  2,909</p>
<p>  Costs, Operating Expenses	  1,697		  2,114</p>
<p>Income before taxes, interests</p>
<p>   royalties, other expenses	 4,609		  5,762</p>
<p>  Income before taxes, royalties   4,749		  5,768</p>
<p>  Taxes, Royalties		     4,111		  5,182</p>
<p>  Net Income				 638		    586</p>
<p>  Oper Income pre Taxes/Royalties  4,089		  5,062</p>
<p>  Pemex Exploration &amp; Production   3,908		  5,219</p>
<p>  Pemex Refinacion			  17		  (136)</p>
<p>  Pemex Gas				   49		   (19)</p>
<p>  Pemex Petrochemicals		   114		    (1)</p>
<p>Legend: Statement is unaudited, *includes consumer taxes.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903. E-mail at timna.tanners@reuters.com))</p>
</text>
